IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-members`
IMPORT `coa3-part8-inspection`
IMPORT `coa-proc-register-copy`

-- coa-proc-register-copy-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-register-copy.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 116 to 118).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- A trace is built on working days: day 0 is the day the company receives the request, AT 5 is the fifth working day.

§ `Tests for the register-copy procedure`

§§ `Fixtures: the request (what s 116(4) asks for, one field per limb)`

-- the request fields, in order: the person is an individual; the name and address is given; the purpose is stated; the request says whether
-- the information will be disclosed to another person; it will be disclosed; the other person is an individual; the other person's name and
-- address is given; the other person's purpose is stated.
`a complete request that discloses to no one` MEANS `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a request that states no purpose` MEANS `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a request that discloses to another person but names no one` MEANS `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a request that discloses to another person and gives everything` MEANS `s 116(4) request for inspection or a copy` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§§ `Assertions: the gate (s 116 and s 117(1))`

-- s 116(1)(a): a member inspects without charge.
#ASSERT `ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 116(1)(b): a person who is not a member inspects on payment of the fee.
#ASSERT `ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 116(2): any person requires a copy on payment of the fee.
#ASSERT `ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- s 116(4)(d): a request that discloses to another person and gives that person's name, address and purpose contains what is required.
#ASSERT `ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a request that discloses to another person and gives everything`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 116(4)(c): no purpose stated.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a request that states no purpose`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 116(4)(d)(i) to (iii): disclosure to another person, whom the request does not name.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a request that discloses to another person but names no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 116(1)(b): a person who is not a member and does not pay the fee has no right to inspect.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 116(2): no fee, no copy.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 116(2A): a restriction under s 120A takes the case outside what is encoded.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 116-118 the company has received a request that section 116 allows` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

§§ `Traces: s 117(1), the five working days`

-- s 117(1)(a): complied with on day 3, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 3

-- s 117(1)(a): complied with on day 5, the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 5

-- s 117(1)(a): complied with on day 6, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 6

-- s 117(1): the company does nothing and the five working days pass.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 6)

-- s 117(1)(a): a person who is not a member asks for a copy and pays the fee; the company complies on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 5

-- s 117(1): the request states no purpose, so it is not a request under s 116 and no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a request that states no purpose`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 116(1)(b): a person who is not a member does not pay the fee, so no right to inspect and no duty arises.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 116(2A): a restriction under s 120A applies, so no duty is encoded.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 117(1)(b), applying to the court`

-- s 117(1)(b): the company applies to the court on day 2, in time; the duty to respond is met.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court` AT 2

-- s 117(1)(b): the company applies on day 5, the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court` AT 5

-- s 117(1)(b): the company applies on day 6, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 117(1) the company's duty to comply with a request or apply to the court` (`a complete request that discloses to no one`) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(b) the company applies to the court` AT 6

§§ `Traces: s 117(2), the notice (day 0 is the day the company applies to the court)`

-- s 117(2): the company notifies the person on day 1.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(2) the company's duty to notify the person making the request` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(2) the company notifies the person making the request that it has applied to the court` AT 1

-- s 117(2): the company has applied and has not notified by day 30; the Act gives no time for the notice, so it stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 117(2) the company's duty to notify the person making the request` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 117(2): the company has not applied to the court, so it owes no notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(2) the company's duty to notify the person making the request` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 117(3)(a), the court's direction (day 0 is the day the company applies to the court)`

-- s 117(3)(a): the court is satisfied that the purpose is not proper and directs the company not to comply on day 8.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(3)(a) the court's duty to direct the company not to comply` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the court` DOES `s 117(3)(a) the court directs the company not to comply with the request` AT 8

-- s 117(3)(a): the court is satisfied and has not directed by day 30; the Act gives the court no time, so the direction stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 117(3)(a) the court's duty to direct the company not to comply` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 117(3): the court is not satisfied that the purpose is improper, so it has no duty to direct.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(3)(a) the court's duty to direct the company not to comply` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 117(3): no application has been made, so the court has no duty to direct.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(3)(a) the court's duty to direct the company not to comply` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 117(5), comply immediately (day 0 is the day of the court's decision or of the discontinuance)`

-- s 117(5): the court has given its decision without directing the company not to comply; the company complies on day 0, immediately.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(5) the company's duty to comply immediately` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 0

-- s 117(5): the same, but the company complies on day 1, the day after the decision, which is not immediately.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 117(5) the company's duty to comply immediately` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 117(1)(a) the company complies with the request by allowing the inspection or providing the copy` AT 1

-- s 117(5): the proceedings are discontinued (the court gives no direction) and the company has not complied by day 2.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 117(5) the company's duty to comply immediately` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 2)

-- s 117(5): the court directed the company not to comply, so there is no duty to comply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(5) the company's duty to comply immediately` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 2)

-- s 117(5): the court has not yet given its decision and the proceedings continue, so the duty has not arisen.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 117(5) the company's duty to comply immediately` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 2)

§§ `Traces: s 118(1), the offence`

-- s 118(1)(a): the company refuses the inspection on day 6, not in accordance with an order of the court.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 118(1)(a) the company's duty not to refuse an inspection or make default in providing a copy` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 118(1) the company refuses the inspection or makes default in providing the copy` AT 6

-- s 118(1)(a): the company has not refused; the prohibition stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 118(1)(a) the company's duty not to refuse an inspection or make default in providing a copy` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 118(1): "otherwise than in accordance with an order of the court": the refusal is in accordance with an order, so no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 118(1)(a) the company's duty not to refuse an inspection or make default in providing a copy` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 118(1) the company refuses the inspection or makes default in providing the copy` AT 6

-- s 118(1)(b): an officer in default.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 118(1)(b) the officer's duty not to be in default in a refusal or default` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 118(1)(b) the officer is in default in the refusal or default` AT 7

-- s 118(1)(b): an officer who is not in default (s 1121) commits no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 118(1)(b) the officer's duty not to be in default in a refusal or default` FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 118(1)(b) the officer is in default in the refusal or default` AT 7

-- s 118(1)(a) and (b): the company refuses and the officer is in default, both on day 6.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 118(1) the company and every officer in default` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 118(1) the company refuses the inspection or makes default in providing the copy` AT 6
    PARTY `ss 116-118 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 118(1)(b) the officer is in default in the refusal or default` AT 6

-- s 118(1)(a): the company refuses on day 6 and nothing is said of the officer; the company has committed the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 118(1) the company and every officer in default` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the company` DOES `s 118(1) the company refuses the inspection or makes default in providing the copy` AT 6

-- s 118(1): no refusal or default yet; both prohibitions stay open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 118(1) the company and every officer in default` FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: s 118(3), the court may compel`

-- s 118(3): inspection is refused, not in accordance with an order; the court orders an immediate inspection on day 9.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 118(3) the court's power to compel an inspection or direct that the copy be sent` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 116-118 the court` DOES `s 118(3) the court orders an immediate inspection or directs that the copy be sent to the person requesting it` AT 9

-- s 118(3): inspection is refused; the court has not ordered by day 30; the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 118(3) the court's power to compel an inspection or direct that the copy be sent` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 118(3): there has been no refusal or default, so the court has no power under this subsection.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 118(3) the court's power to compel an inspection or direct that the copy be sent` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 118(3): the refusal was in accordance with an order of the court ("any such refusal or default"), so no power to compel.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 118(3) the court's power to compel an inspection or direct that the copy be sent` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- No trace in this file differs in class (FULFILLED, BREACH, RESIDUAL) between the unstable build (a50cbd0, 25 November 2026) and main (112):
-- all 35 traces match their EXPECT on both. The Result block prints differently on main in six traces, all with the same class on both:
--   * the three traces of `s 117(1)` that breach (complied with on day 6; nothing done by day 6; applied on day 6): the ROR has two alternatives and
--     both breach; unstable joins the two breaches with BY under one BREACH, main joins them with OR DEONTIC BREACHED.
--   * the two traces with no refusal yet (`s 118(1)(a)` and `s 118(1)`): unstable prints the open prohibition's LEST with its BREACH in parentheses, main without.
--   * the `s 118(1)` trace in which the company refuses and the officer is in default on day 6 (a RAND of two breaches): unstable prints both breaches
--     (the company's and the officer's); main prints only the company's. The class is BREACH on both.
